warning[pointer_lifetime]: `p` refers to an element in `a` whose identity is invalidated on every path to this use
  --> tests/lint/pointer_lifetime/movement/bad.jai:20:10
   |
 7 | ordered :: (a: *[..] int, i: int) {} @RemovesFromArray(ordered,1)
   |            ------------------------- invalidation inferred through this call
   ...
18 |     p := *a[3];
   |          ----- pointer derived here
19 |     ordered(*a, 1);
   |     -------------- `a` element moved or removed here
20 |     sink(p);
   |          ^ pointer used here after its element was moved or removed
   |
   = help: take the pointer again after the operation, or keep a stable key instead
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/pointer_lifetime

